### StageSync API HTTP Requests (VSCode REST Client / JetBrains HTTP Client)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@eventId = evt_technova_2025
@keynoteId = agt_keynote

### 1. Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 2. Get Consolidated Event State (Simulate Live Time at Keynote)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/state?at=2025-09-19T04:15:00.000Z

### 3. List All Speakers
GET {{baseUrl}}/speakers?eventId={{eventId}}

### 4. List Agenda in Chronological Order
GET {{baseUrl}}/agenda?eventId={{eventId}}

### 5. Preview 15-Minute Cascade Delay (Zero Writes to DB)
POST {{baseUrl}}/agenda/{{keynoteId}}/delay/preview
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "delayMinutes": 15,
  "cascade": true,
  "reason": "Dr. Rohan Verma flight delayed from Mumbai"
}

### 6. Apply 15-Minute Cascade Delay (With Idempotency Key)
POST {{baseUrl}}/agenda/{{keynoteId}}/delay
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-keynote-delay-001

{
  "delayMinutes": 15,
  "cascade": true,
  "reason": "Dr. Rohan Verma flight delayed from Mumbai"
}

### 7. Re-send Same Idempotency Key (Returns Idempotent-Replay: true header)
POST {{baseUrl}}/agenda/{{keynoteId}}/delay
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-keynote-delay-001

{
  "delayMinutes": 15,
  "cascade": true,
  "reason": "Dr. Rohan Verma flight delayed from Mumbai"
}

### 8. View Schedule Change History
GET {{baseUrl}}/schedule-changes?eventId={{eventId}}

### 9. Get Recovery Options & Slack for AI Prompt [STRETCH]
GET {{baseUrl}}/agenda/{{keynoteId}}/recovery-options?delayMinutes=15

### 10. Test Overlap Refusal (cascade=false -> 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/agenda/{{keynoteId}}/delay
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "delayMinutes": 15,
  "cascade": false,
  "reason": "Will cause overlap"
}

### 11. Test Midnight Refusal (delay crosses midnight -> 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/agenda/{{keynoteId}}/delay
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "delayMinutes": 900,
  "cascade": true,
  "reason": "Pushes past midnight"
}

### 12. Reset Demo State Back to Pristine TechNova Seed
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reset
